      "message": "Changes adding and removing tens or even hundreds of lines of code that are 95% similar are very hard to review as the differences are easy to miss; for example, this `unsafe` was removed without explanation (and arguably wrongly).\n\nAs we\u0027ve already reviewed quite a few CLs of this nature and as we\u0027ll have to move a good chunk of the code from `pvmfw/` to `vmbase/` for re-use, may I ask you to start splitting changes like this one in:\n\n1. a commit that renames the files, limiting changes to what\u0027s absolutely necessary to prevent the build from breaking\n1. one or more commits that apply the extra modifications/clean-up you consider necessary\n\n? This will result in a less clobbered history (`git-blame`) as 1. will make Git aware of the file being moved, while 2. will lead to a better review process (and code quality) by allowing reviewers to easily identify those small differences.",
